stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> Free

    Free --> Reserved: reservation created (future capability)
    Reserved --> Free: reservation expired or cancelled
    Reserved --> Occupied: VehicleEntered matches reservation

    Free --> Occupied: VehicleEntered<br/>point-in-polygon match, track_id assigned

    Occupied --> Occupied: VehicleRelocated<br/>same track_id, new slot
    Occupied --> Free: VehicleRelocated<br/>this slot becomes the OLD slot, ParkingHistory row written

    Occupied --> Exited: VehicleExited<br/>track_id leaves site, plate confirmed at exit gate
    Exited --> Free: slot released, current_vehicle_id cleared

    Free --> Disabled: TENANT_ADMIN marks slot out of service
    Occupied --> Disabled: forced maintenance override (rare, admin action)
    Disabled --> Free: TENANT_ADMIN re-enables slot

    note right of Occupied
        ParkingSlot.status = occupied
        Vehicle.current_slot_id set
        Emits VehicleEntered or VehicleRelocated
    end note

    note right of Free
        ParkingSlot.status = free
        current_vehicle_id = null
    end note

    note left of Reserved
        TARGET-ONLY. Reservation is a future
        capability, not in the initial scope.
        Today's code has no ParkingSlot,
        no reservation, no occupancy concept.
    end note
